---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Roy Li | Seeking the BC Conservative nomination in Vancouver-Langara">
  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow light">Vancouver-Langara · British Columbia</div>
          <h1>A builder’s voice for <em>Vancouver-Langara.</em></h1>
          <p class="lead">I’m Roy Li — a tech entrepreneur, a Vancouver resident, and a father. I’m seeking the BC Conservative nomination in Vancouver-Langara because our community deserves safer streets, honest budgets, and a government that works for people, not bureaucrats.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/about/">Meet Roy</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="/ideas/">Read my priorities</a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-meta">中文信息请见 <a href="/zh/">中文版页面</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="portrait-wrap">
          <div class="portrait-accent"></div>
          <div class="portrait-frame">
            <img src="/portrait.jpg" alt="Roy Li" width="814" height="1086" />
          </div>
          <div class="portrait-tag">
            <strong>Roy Li</strong>
            <span>Nomination candidate</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Fact strip -->
    <section class="strip">
      <div class="strip-inner">
        <div class="strip-item">
          <div class="num">01</div>
          <div><strong>Safer communities</strong><p>Safe streets, safe transit, and safe neighbourhoods come first.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-item">
          <div class="num">02</div>
          <div><strong>Balanced budgets</strong><p>Today’s deficits become tomorrow’s taxes. Government must live within reality.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-item">
          <div class="num">03</div>
          <div><strong>Less red tape</strong><p>Make it easier to invest, hire, build, and stay in British Columbia.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Statement -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="statement">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Why I’m running</div>
            <h2>Vancouver-Langara deserves a serious, practical voice in Victoria.</h2>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p>I have spent my career building companies — hiring people, meeting payroll, raising capital, and making decisions where the consequences are real. That experience taught me something simple: confidence is not created by speeches. It is created by predictable rules, disciplined budgets, safe communities, and a government that respects the people who work, invest, and raise families here.</p>
            <p>British Columbia has lost that confidence. Families feel unsafe, businesses feel punished, and government spends as if consequences do not exist. I’m seeking the BC Conservative nomination in Vancouver-Langara to help change that.</p>
            <div class="signature">— Roy Li</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About -->
    <section class="section tight" id="about" style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="wrap about-split">
        <div class="about-photo">
          <img src="/portrait.jpg" alt="Roy Li" width="814" height="1086" />
        </div>
        <div class="about-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">About Roy</div>
          <h2 style="font-size:clamp(30px,3.4vw,44px);line-height:1.1;margin:0 0 20px">Entrepreneur. Builder. Neighbour.</h2>
          <p>Roy Li is a technology entrepreneur whose background spans software, capital markets, and building companies through uncertainty. He leads a publicly listed technology company and has spent years working with founders, investors, and employees who chose to build in British Columbia.</p>
          <p>He lives in Vancouver with his family, and believes the province can be compassionate without being careless — investing in the future without ignoring the budget, and supporting vulnerable people while still defending public order.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li><span>Background</span>Technology entrepreneur and CEO</li>
            <li><span>Home</span>Vancouver, British Columbia</li>
            <li><span>Seeking</span>BC Conservative nomination, Vancouver-Langara</li>
            <li><span>Focus</span>Public safety, fiscal discipline, enterprise</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top:30px">
            <a class="button navy" href="/about/">Full profile</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/roy-li-2a4248217/" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Priorities -->
    <section class="section" id="priorities" style="background:var(--paper-2)">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head center">
          <div class="eyebrow">Priorities</div>
          <h2>Common sense for British Columbia.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Restore public safety, balance the budget, cut red tape, and get B.C. working again. These are the principles Roy will bring to Vancouver-Langara.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <article class="card">
            <div class="index">01</div>
            <h3>Restore public safety</h3>
            <p>Public safety is the basic promise of government. Families should feel safe in their neighbourhoods, seniors in public spaces, and small businesses should not be left to absorb repeat offences on their own.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <div class="index">02</div>
            <h3>Balance the budget</h3>
            <p>Balanced budgets are a moral commitment to the next generation. When government spends beyond its means, ordinary people pay through higher taxes, weaker services, and fewer opportunities.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <div class="index">03</div>
            <h3>Cut red tape, back enterprise</h3>
            <p>Builders go where rules are clear and costs are realistic. B.C. should make it easier to invest, hire, build, and stay here — for the family business and the tech startup alike.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <div class="index">04</div>
            <h3>Work for people, not bureaucrats</h3>
            <p>What is the problem? What does it cost? Who pays? What result should we expect? Good government answers those questions in plain language and is accountable for the results.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align:center;margin-top:36px">
          <a class="button secondary" href="/ideas/">Read the full priorities</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Langara band -->
    <section class="band" id="langara">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow light">Vancouver-Langara</div>
          <h2>A community worth fighting for.</h2>
          <p>Vancouver-Langara is home to families, seniors, students, professionals, small-business owners, homeowners, renters, and newcomers — people who care about safety, affordability, opportunity, and responsible government.</p>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>Safe streets, safe transit, and safe neighbourhoods</li>
            <li>Respect for families, seniors, and taxpayers</li>
            <li>A stronger environment for local business, jobs, and innovation</li>
            <li>Real accountability from the provincial government</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top:30px">
            <a class="button primary" href="/langara/">About the riding</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <blockquote>
          “A province cannot build confidence if families feel unsafe, businesses feel punished, and government spends as if consequences do not exist.”
          <cite>Roy Li</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Connect -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">Follow along</div>
          <h2>Ideas, notes, and updates.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">Roy shares his thinking on responsible government, public safety, balanced budgets, technology, and business.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="links-grid">
          <a class="link-card" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/roy-li-2a4248217/" rel="noopener">
            <strong>LinkedIn</strong>
            <p>Professional background and regular updates.</p>
            <span class="arrow">View profile →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="link-card" href="/notes/">
            <strong>Notes</strong>
            <p>Short essays on British Columbia, business, public safety, and responsible government.</p>
            <span class="arrow">Read notes →</span>
          </a>
          <a class="link-card" href="/contact/">
            <strong>Community conversations</strong>
            <p>Speaking, media, or a conversation in Vancouver-Langara.</p>
            <span class="arrow">Get in touch →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Let’s build a stronger Vancouver-Langara.</h2>
            <p>Share the issues that matter to you, ask a question, or lend your support as Roy seeks the BC Conservative nomination.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cta-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact Roy</a>
            <a class="button ghost" href="mailto:roy@xdt.com">Email</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
